Retro-audit of defect eight (sonnet's demand), done mechanically
----------------------------------------------------------------

Per committed build, fuel representation vs guard family, from
git show <commit>:research.py --

  460431a  nat fuel   NatEq/NatPred guards   Tail(fuel): absent
  c2d890c  nat fuel   NatEq/NatPred guards   Tail(fuel): absent
  28e43f7  nat fuel   NatEq/NatPred guards   Tail(fuel): absent
  0770b9d  nat fuel   NatEq/NatPred guards   Tail(fuel): absent
  fe26dc8  nat fuel   NatEq/NatPred guards   Tail(fuel): absent
  76f4389  chain fuel zero NatEq(fuel        Tail(fuel): guarded

The broken hybrid -- chain fuel behind a NatEq guard -- existed only
in the uncommitted working tree during the defect-eight turn and was
caught by the test battery before any commit and before any session.
Every logged session ran on an internally consistent engine; the
walk-off-the-chain failure was never reachable in any evidence build.
Consistency of the fuel machinery is what this audit certifies --
nothing more; other defects remain findable only by running.

Set B, restated per sonnet's correction
---------------------------------------

Three class-A outcomes were not three calibration successes; they were
two findings wearing one label:

1. The ground factorization policy cannot transfer to symbolic
   exponents -- and one level deeper, post-evaluator it cannot even
   form, since its training residuals are discharged before becoming
   requests. Regime C on this substrate builds from non-ground
   episodes only.
2. The pack library holds no rule whose conclusion or premise shape
   can foothold on research-grammar goals at all: a coverage gap
   (vocabulary disjointness), not a search-depth gap.

B1 diagnosis, sonnet's three-way question answered: option (3), with a
correction to its premise. The exponent-algebra law of Experiment 1
was never in a pack -- it was live-taught in a session whose state was
deliberately not carried (session hygiene). The library genuinely
lacks the rule, and additionally cannot express it toward research
goals across the vocabulary boundary. Prescription applied: teach that
specific rule live, rerun B1 alone, confirm Regime B before B2/B3 are
reconsidered. Experiment 4 stays unrun.

Corrections after sol's review of the third cut
-----------------------------------------------

1. Precision: B1 found REFLEXIVITY, not transport. The residual
   (eq (times k m) (times k m)) is symbolic self-equality; transport
   means moving a property across an equality -- Eq(a,b), P(a) -> P(b).
   The B1 log's phrase "transport-shaped" was too loose; the precise
   statement is: the machine found a missing symbolic reflexivity
   premise required by a goal-directed power-decomposition rule.
   B1 = reflexivity; B2 = substitutivity/transport; B3 = no-solutions
   transport. Three different logical forms, calibrated separately.

2. Invariant provenance, read precisely. An adopted (Invariant ...)
   record audited under INVENTED_LEMMA means exactly three things and
   no more: the observable SHAPE came from the fixed trainer-supplied
   library; the CONJECTURE came from trace evidence the machine
   checked; the ADOPTION came from the operator. The machine verified
   and selected; it did not invent the observable. Trace-compression
   candidates, by contrast, are anti-unified from the machine's own
   traces end to end.

3. Sol's ground transport probe collides with the evaluator by
   design: (divides 3 (plus 3 3)) is ground-decidable and closes by
   evaluation without touching any transport law. Transport is
   testable only on symbolic instances on this substrate; the B2/B3
   sessions use them, and the ground version is run once to show the
   evaluator doing exactly what it should.
